# TTP-2026-0141 — Internal AD Kill-Chain: Poisoning → Offline Crack → Credential Validation → WinRM Lateral (SIM-ITDR-015)
# XQL paste-buffer generated by detection_scanner/scripts/export_artifacts.py

## BIOC — ITDR-015 Null-Session Directory Enumeration Against Domain Controller
# severity: medium
# A single source host issues a burst of SAMR/LSARPC directory-object reads against a Domain Controller (users, groups, domain policy) consistent with enum4linux-ng AD enumeration. The CGO here is the operator recon shell on the attacker foothold; this is the opening move of the kill chain.

dataset = msft_windows_security
| filter event_id in (4661, 4662) and object_type in ("SAM_USER", "SAM_GROUP", "SAM_DOMAIN")
| comp count() as dir_reads, count_distinct(object_name) as objects by ip_address, account_name
| filter objects >= 10
| fields ip_address, account_name, dir_reads, objects

## BIOC — ITDR-015 SMB Share Enumeration And Permission Mapping
# severity: medium
# A single source enumerates many SMB shares and maps their read/write permissions on the lab file/DC hosts (smbmap), a share-discovery burst that widens the attacker's picture of reachable data before credential capture.

dataset = msft_windows_security
| filter event_id in (5140, 5145)
| comp count_distinct(share_name) as shares, count() as accesses by ip_address, account_name
| filter shares >= 5
| fields ip_address, account_name, shares, accesses

## BIOC — ITDR-015 Offline Credential-Cracking Tool Execution With Recon-Shell Lineage
# severity: high
# An offline password-cracking binary (john or hashcat) executes on the attacker foothold with its causality actor rooted in the operator recon shell (or the responder capture process) — the offline-crack leg of the chain. Keying on causality_actor_process_command_line ties the crack to the same lineage that ran the enumeration and poisoning.

dataset = xdr_data
| filter event_type = ENUM.PROCESS and event_sub_type = ENUM.PROCESS_START
| filter action_process_image_name in ("john", "hashcat")
| filter causality_actor_process_image_name in ("bash", "zsh", "sh", "responder")
| fields agent_hostname, actor_effective_username, causality_actor_process_command_line, causality_actor_process_image_name, action_process_image_name

## BIOC — ITDR-015 Compromised-Account Authentication From Attacker Foothold
# severity: high
# The cracked domain credential is replayed from the attacker foothold IP, producing successful network logons across two or more distinct domain hosts in a short window (netexec validation spray). Same-source, single-account fan-out across hosts is the credential-validation signature bridging the crack to lateral movement.

dataset = msft_windows_security
| filter event_id = 4624 and logon_type = 3
| comp count_distinct(computer_name) as hosts, count() as logons by ip_address, account_name
| filter hosts >= 2
| fields ip_address, account_name, hosts, logons

## BIOC — ITDR-015 WinRM Lateral Movement Landing Remote Shell
# severity: high
# A WinRM service host (wsmprovhost.exe) spawns an interactive shell (cmd.exe/powershell.exe) on a domain host — the endpoint-side landing of an evil-winrm lateral session. causality_actor_process_image_name = wsmprovhost.exe is the stitch between the inbound WinRM network session and the remote shell it lands.

dataset = xdr_data
| filter event_type = ENUM.PROCESS and event_sub_type = ENUM.PROCESS_START
| filter causality_actor_process_image_name = "wsmprovhost.exe"
| filter action_process_image_name in ("cmd.exe", "powershell.exe", "conhost.exe")
| fields agent_hostname, causality_actor_process_command_line, action_process_image_name

## ABIOC — ITDR-015 Rogue LLMNR And NBT-NS Responder With NetNTLMv2 Capture (behavioral-ML, causality-anchored)
# severity: high
# behavioral_profile: machine-learning
# causality_anchor: Learned per-host name-resolution baseline (which hosts legitimately answer LLMNR/NBT-NS and for which names); the rogue responder deviates by authoritatively answering a spike of distinct names it never previously owned and drawing inbound NetNTLMv2 auth.
# A host on the segment begins authoritatively answering LLMNR (UDP 5355) and NBT-NS (UDP 137) broadcast name queries for names it has never legitimately owned, then receives inbound NetNTLMv2 authentication — the behavioral signature of a rogue Responder poisoning names to harvest hashes. The ABIOC anchors on the learned per-host name-resolution baseline: the responder host deviates by suddenly resolving a spike of distinct names.

dataset = xdr_data
| filter event_type = ENUM.NETWORK
| filter action_local_port in (137, 5355) or action_remote_port in (137, 5355)
| comp count() as name_responses, count_distinct(dns_query_name) as names by agent_hostname, action_local_ip
| filter name_responses >= 10 and names >= 5
| fields agent_hostname, action_local_ip, name_responses, names

## VALIDATION — ITDR-015 SMB RPC LDAP Enumeration Fan-Out To Domain Controller
# purpose: validation
# dataset: panw_ngfw_traffic_raw

dataset = panw_ngfw_traffic_raw
| filter _time > to_timestamp(current_time() - 1800)
| filter flow_direction = "inbound" and dst_port in (135, 139, 389, 445, 636)
| comp count() as conns, count_distinct(dst_port) as ports by src_ip, dst_ip
| filter ports >= 3 and conns >= 20
| sort desc conns
| fields src_ip, dst_ip, ports, conns

## VALIDATION — ITDR-015 SMB Share-Enumeration Fan-Out From Single Source
# purpose: validation
# dataset: msft_windows_security

dataset = msft_windows_security
| filter _time > to_timestamp(current_time() - 1800)
| filter event_id = 5140
| comp count_distinct(share_name) as shares, count() as accesses by ip_address, account_name
| filter shares >= 5
| sort desc shares
| fields ip_address, account_name, shares, accesses

## VALIDATION — ITDR-015 Inbound NetNTLMv2 Authentication To Rogue Responder Host
# purpose: validation
# dataset: panw_ngfw_traffic_raw

dataset = panw_ngfw_traffic_raw
| filter _time > to_timestamp(current_time() - 1800)
| filter dst_port in (137, 139, 445, 5355)
| comp count() as sessions, count_distinct(src_ip) as victims by dst_ip
| filter victims >= 1 and sessions >= 1
| sort desc sessions
| fields dst_ip, victims, sessions

## VALIDATION — ITDR-015 Offline Cracking-Tool Process With Recon-Shell Causality
# purpose: validation
# dataset: xdr_data

dataset = xdr_data
| filter event_type = ENUM.PROCESS and event_sub_type = ENUM.PROCESS_START
| filter action_process_image_name in ("john", "hashcat")
| filter causality_actor_process_image_name in ("bash", "zsh", "sh", "responder")
| comp count() as crack_procs by agent_hostname, actor_effective_username, causality_actor_process_image_name, action_process_image_name
| filter crack_procs >= 1
| fields agent_hostname, actor_effective_username, causality_actor_process_image_name, action_process_image_name, crack_procs

## VALIDATION — ITDR-015 Compromised-Account Validation Across Domain Hosts
# purpose: validation
# dataset: msft_windows_security

dataset = msft_windows_security
| filter _time > to_timestamp(current_time() - 1800)
| filter event_id in (4624, 4625) and logon_type = 3
| comp count_distinct(computer_name) as hosts, count() as attempts by ip_address, account_name
| filter hosts >= 2
| sort desc hosts
| fields ip_address, account_name, hosts, attempts

## VALIDATION — ITDR-015 WinRM Remote-Shell Session Landing On Domain Host
# purpose: validation
# dataset: xdr_data

dataset = xdr_data
| filter event_type = ENUM.PROCESS and event_sub_type = ENUM.PROCESS_START
| filter causality_actor_process_image_name = "wsmprovhost.exe"
| filter action_process_image_name in ("cmd.exe", "powershell.exe", "conhost.exe")
| comp count() as shells by agent_hostname, causality_actor_process_image_name, action_process_image_name
| filter shells >= 1
| fields agent_hostname, causality_actor_process_image_name, action_process_image_name, shells

